{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01088",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.73,
      "end_seconds": 5.71,
      "duration_seconds": 4.98,
      "text": "Hello, take a seat, I'll be with you in a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 9.08,
      "end_seconds": 14.62,
      "duration_seconds": 5.54,
      "text": "Hi doctor, I got here as fast as I could."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 16.03,
      "end_seconds": 19.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "What would you like to start with today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 19.96,
      "end_seconds": 26.06,
      "duration_seconds": 6.1,
      "text": "So, I've been waking up at night short of breath, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.24,
      "end_seconds": 31.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "Tell me your medicines, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 32.54,
      "end_seconds": 37.56,
      "duration_seconds": 5.02,
      "text": "Metoprolol. I take it 50 milligrams, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 38.12,
      "end_seconds": 43.65,
      "duration_seconds": 5.53,
      "text": "Yes, carry on. So, has this been going on for long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.22,
      "end_seconds": 46.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "About... well, six months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 47.11,
      "end_seconds": 49.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.91,
      "text": "Anything that improves it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 50.03,
      "end_seconds": 62.78,
      "duration_seconds": 12.75,
      "text": "Only sitting up, and it's not much. There's breathlessness when I lie flat as well. About breathlessness when I lie flat, lying flat definitely sets it off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.31,
      "end_seconds": 83.28,
      "duration_seconds": 4.97,
      "text": "A few quick ones: coughing up blood, chest pain or calf pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.82,
      "end_seconds": 94.49,
      "duration_seconds": 5.67,
      "text": "I haven't had coughing up blood, chest pain or calf pain, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.89,
      "end_seconds": 99.94,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "Any change in your bowel habit or your stomach generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.4,
      "end_seconds": 103.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Bowels are regular, nothing odd."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.79,
      "end_seconds": 125.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "Let's talk a little about your daily life and habits."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.51,
      "end_seconds": 140.38,
      "duration_seconds": 13.87,
      "text": "I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day. Not much, I mostly stay in these days. I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 142.29,
      "end_seconds": 147.84,
      "duration_seconds": 5.55,
      "text": "So, what conditions have you been treated for in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.2,
      "end_seconds": 158.86,
      "duration_seconds": 6.66,
      "text": "I've had heart failure, yes. I did try to ignore it for a while."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.75,
      "end_seconds": 165.08,
      "duration_seconds": 5.33,
      "text": "Yes, heart failure is known to us, good to have that clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.76,
      "end_seconds": 178.06,
      "duration_seconds": 5.3,
      "text": "Are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 178.6,
      "end_seconds": 182.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "Kiwi. I come out in... well, hives."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 199.68,
      "end_seconds": 212.13,
      "duration_seconds": 12.45,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Height 154 centimetres, saturation 90 percent, respiratory rate 21, pressure 130 over 72, weight 83 kilos, temperature 37.3, heart rate 88."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 214.1,
      "end_seconds": 215.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.42,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.95,
      "end_seconds": 220.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "Right, let's have a proper look at you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 225.9,
      "end_seconds": 226.9,
      "duration_seconds": 1.0,
      "text": "Sure thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.57,
      "end_seconds": 231.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "Raise your arm for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.05,
      "end_seconds": 247.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "Neck veins are raised."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.62,
      "end_seconds": 263.62,
      "duration_seconds": 13.0,
      "text": "You can sit up now. Putting it all together, I don't have a clear answer today: fluid overload related to the heart is possible, and so is a chest infection."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 264.96,
      "end_seconds": 267.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "Do you think it's something serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.18,
      "end_seconds": 291.88,
      "duration_seconds": 22.7,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with fluid overload related to the heart do well once it's treated properly. Let me repeat that back to make sure. You've been waking up at night short of breath for six months, and no chest pain or coughing up blood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 293.02,
      "end_seconds": 295.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "Yes, you've got it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 298.99,
      "end_seconds": 323.69,
      "duration_seconds": 24.7,
      "text": "We should do a chest X-ray for breathlessness. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more. For this, furosemide, 40 milligrams, every morning, until we review. You take it by mouth. It's for fluid overload. Weigh yourself every morning, and tell us if you put on more than two kilos in a few days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 324.24,
      "end_seconds": 330.02,
      "duration_seconds": 5.78,
      "text": "I see, go ahead. Is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 331.98,
      "end_seconds": 334.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "I think I understand everything. Thanks."
    }
  ]
}